 "result": "Per the subagent's report, three tests clearly fail for other reasons, and one is unconfirmed:\n\n1. **`tests/test_request.py::test_limit_config`**: `Request.max_form_memory_size` is `None` where the test expects `500000`. The subagent attributes this to Werkzeug 3.0.3 behaving differently, so it is a version mismatch, but a different one from the `partitioned` keyword.\n\n2. **`tests/test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`**: raises `RuntimeError: Install Tessel with the 'async' extra in order to use async views.` The async dependency (probably `asgiref`) isn't installed.\n\n3. **`tests/test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`**: fails with a `pytest.PytestWarning`/pytest error. The subagent did not inspect it, so the cause is unknown, though it looks environment-related.\n\n4. **`tests/test_reqctx.py::test_session_dynamic_cookie_name`** (unconfirmed): it returns an HTML error page instead of `b'value set'`. It is probably the `partitioned` `TypeError` surfacing as a 500, but the subagent didn't verify that, so it may or may not belong to the main cause.\n\nThe count is slightly loose too. The subagent said \"about 20\" failures come from the main cause, and the named lists give 19, plus this fourth test makes 20. The 24 failures are therefore roughly 20 from the main cause and 3 or 4 from the others.",
